   - Four Rules of Simple Design + Absolute Priority Premise (APP) mass scoring — used by the refactor subagent; Rule 2 (reveals intent) explicitly trumps APP mass.
   - **IEEE-754 float hazard (load-bearing)**: `100 * 1.1 === 110.00000000000001`. The premium must use the additive form `policyBase + policyBase * RATE`, never `policyBase * 1.1`. The final `Math.ceil` **amplifies** this error (115.00000000000001 → 116 instead of 115). A comment in the source records this; it must not be "simplified".
   - Domain modelling: item-specific modifiers (cursed, high enchantment) charge against the affected item's own base premium; policy-wide modifiers (first insurance, loyalty, follow-up) charge against the sum of all item base premiums; the 5 G processing fee is added at the very end; premiums round up, payouts round down.

