   - Distinguished tests that *drive* new code from tests that *characterise* already-satisfied behaviour. Of the 22 tests activated this session, only 4 required a Green phase (follow-up discount, first claim, enchantment-halving clause, cap exhaustion). For the other 18 I predicted a pass, reported it honestly, ran no Green phase, and continued — while noting the counterfactual each test would catch (e.g. policy-wide curse would give 261 not 231; one-deductible-per-incident would give 700 not 600; symmetric grouping in `insuranceSum` would give 3200 not 3500).
